Father Bob was really happy to find a +3 axe named Cleaver on level 3!
Then his little dog named K9 got polymorphed into a baby black dragon on
level 10; after the confusion this polymorphing must have caused
K9, Father Bob didn't have the heart to change his name to something
more appropriate to his new form.  Just as well: on the first maze
level, the (now adult) dragon was polymorphed again, this time
into an earth elemental -- what do you call an earth elemental?!
Now, K9 can easily follow his beloved master through the mazes by
phasing through the walls!

Dave Paoletti :)

minor spoiler...

If your pet is polymorhped by a trap, and you REALLY like his new
form and don't want him to be changed into something different/useless,
drop (or throw, if you don't have magic resistance) a cursed item
on top of the trap and your pet will never step onto it again!


